WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.140
Castle's unexpected cancellation&nbsp;
nearly left fans and the creative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:07.848
team with nothing but a cliffhanger.&nbsp;
What the heck happened and why?

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:12.240
The writers of Castle planned on getting the&nbsp;
greenlight for Season 9. Because of this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.720
they created a story where Beckett and&nbsp;
Castle are attacked and gunned down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.380
in their home. The season was meant&nbsp;
to end with both Castle and Beckett&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:22.500
lying in a pool of their own blood,&nbsp;
with their fate left up in the air.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.920
While that would have made for a&nbsp;
good season finale, the fate of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.640
the cliffhanger was already revealed.&nbsp;
Beckett would succumb to her injuries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:35.839
as Stana Katic was not slated to return for Season&nbsp;
9. The actress had been unceremoniously fired.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:37.859
"Goodnight, Castle."

00:00:42.262 --> 00:00:45.780
This came as a surprise. The entire&nbsp;
premise of the series was built around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.721
the relationship between Castle and Beckett.

00:00:47.721 --> 00:00:56.739
"I'm still amazed at the depths of your&nbsp;
strength and your heart. And your hotness."

00:00:56.739 --> 00:01:01.200
It's because of her that there are murders to&nbsp;
solve at all. Katic's firing wasn't received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:06.620
positively by long-time Castle fans, as the entire&nbsp;
point of the show would change with her death.

00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:10.599
"You're the best that I've ever&nbsp;
trained. Maybe the best I've ever seen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.960
But you weren't having any&nbsp;
fun before he came along."

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:19.680
Luckily or not so luckily, depending&nbsp;
on whom you ask, Castle was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.320
canceled, so audiences never&nbsp;
saw a season without Beckett.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:27.360
Before it was revealed that Season 8 would be the&nbsp;
final season for "Castle," the series was gearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:32.100
up to go in an entirely new direction. With&nbsp;
the death of Stana Katic's Detective Beckett,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:36.300
the premise of the show was going to shift. Season&nbsp;
8 had already laid the groundwork for this change,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:40.020
as Castle stopped working with the&nbsp;
NYPD homicide department. In order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.740
to appease his interest in all things&nbsp;
murder, he opens his own PI business,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.800
where his daughter Alexis, played&nbsp;
by Molly Quinn, works with him.

00:01:49.035 --> 00:01:54.017
"Oh my God, this turned out so much&nbsp;
cooler than I thought it would!"

00:01:54.017 --> 00:01:57.420
He's also working with a new female&nbsp;
protagonist, Hayley Shipton, played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:02.521
by Toks Olagundoye, a former MI6 operative&nbsp;
who's moved into the security business.

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:04.920
"Hope you don't mind. I'm just&nbsp;
giving her some PI lessons."

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.980
"Hayley was teaching me the&nbsp;
art of manipulating men."

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:11.280
She was clearly meant to be a Beckett replacement&nbsp;
for the show if it continued into Season 9.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:15.480
According to Entertainment Weekly, had Castle&nbsp;
been renewed, it would have revolved around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.220
Castle's PI business as he hunts his wife's&nbsp;
killer. It's likely that Castle would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:24.720
uncovered a larger conspiracy revolving around&nbsp;
Beckett's death. Everyone in the show would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.260
out for blood, which would allow "Castle"&nbsp;
to include all previous main characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:32.460
such as Detective Javier and Detective&nbsp;
Ryan, in the reconfigured series.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:36.900
Season 9 could have shown how Castle's search&nbsp;
for vengeance would take him down a dark path,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:40.897
but it's likely that, by the end of the season,&nbsp;
Castle would have found some form of closure.

00:02:41.199 --> 00:02:46.240
It's been suggested that Castle stars Nathan&nbsp;
Fillion and Stana Katic didn't get along,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.568
and that friction is why Katic was fired.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:52.763
"Your inspiration might strike&nbsp;
you sooner than you think."

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:57.060
An inside source spilled to Hello!&nbsp;
magazine just how bad the castmates'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:00.420
relationship was. The actors wouldn't&nbsp;
speak to each other outside of filming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:05.340
and Katic could often be found in tears in&nbsp;
her dressing room. According to the insider,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:09.060
the crew encouraged the co-stars to go to&nbsp;
therapy to resolve their intense dislike of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.800
one another. US Weekly also reported the on-set&nbsp;
tension. Another insider claimed that Fillion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:18.419
was horrible to his co-star, while Katic just&nbsp;
wanted to get her job done without complications.

00:03:18.419 --> 00:03:21.359
"Yeah, well, things have never&nbsp;
been easy between you and me."

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.480
While neither Katic nor Fillion has ever commented&nbsp;
on these rumors, the fact that they haven't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:32.786
refuted the reports speaks volumes, especially in&nbsp;
light of Katic's surprise firing from the series.

00:03:32.786 --> 00:03:37.500
Katic was reportedly blindsided by Castle's&nbsp;
decision to terminate her contract. At the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.020
however, the actress remained&nbsp;
professional and didn't comment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:43.740
on her relationship with co-star Nathan&nbsp;
Fillion or the show's sudden ending.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:47.160
After some time had passed, Katic&nbsp;
shared with News Corp. that she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.160
proud of her work on the show and how&nbsp;
special her character, Beckett, was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.800
and that she was hurt and confused by the&nbsp;
way it all ended. She told The Daily Mail,

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.560
"It would be a disservice to the work that I&nbsp;
did, which I feel partly contributed to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.760
success of the show, if I looked back on it and&nbsp;
was anything but grateful for the awesome run."

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.080
Katic shared with Entertainment Weekly that she&nbsp;
found her ending with the series "harsh" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:11.100
that she was still unclear as to what happened&nbsp;
between her and the network. However, she chose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:15.480
to look back fondly on her experience and on&nbsp;
the people that she met while working on set.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:20.822
Just tell us, Stana: what was the drama&nbsp;
between you and Nathan Fillion? Spill the tea!

00:04:20.822 --> 00:04:24.960
Castle executive producer Alexi Hawley says&nbsp;
they always had a contingency plan just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.680
in case the show didn't get renewed.&nbsp;
While Season 8 of Castle was airing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.820
the network had yet to announce there would be&nbsp;
a Season 9. In fact, the cast and crew were not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.900
made aware of the network's decision to pull&nbsp;
the plug until close to the Season 8 finale.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:38.880
Hawley told Entertainment Weekly,

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.060
"If we hear that we're not coming&nbsp;
back, we have shot something that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.540
we can put at the end of the episode as&nbsp;
a way to put a button on everything."

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:49.800
It wasn't something the crew wanted to do.&nbsp;
They were hopeful Castle would be renewed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.980
which would allow the series to tackle&nbsp;
the characters' pursuit of vengeance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:57.360
over Beckett's death. According to Hawley, they&nbsp;
shot a final time jump scene to appease fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:02.220
as they didn't want to leave them with questions,&nbsp;
but co-showrunner Terence Paul Winter shared with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.640
Entertainment Weekly that his "hope [was]&nbsp;
that it [would never see] the light of day."

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:09.840
Sadly, it did. The clip jumps seven&nbsp;
years in the future and features&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.380
voiceovers from Castle and Beckett.&nbsp;
The two are very much alive, thriving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:18.500
and still in love. They even have a house full of&nbsp;
kids, proving that they still make a great team.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:22.920
At the end of Season 6, Castle's original&nbsp;
showrunner, Andrew Marlowe, stepped down.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:26.460
"We have a great lead producer, Andrew Marlowe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:31.320
who loves women. And so I think he loved&nbsp;
letting her shine as a woman in the end."

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:35.760
Marlowe went out with a bang. The Season&nbsp;
6 finale showed Castle being kidnapped on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:39.360
his wedding day. It was a punch to the gut.&nbsp;
Audiences thought they were finally getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.740
a happy ending only to have the dream snatched&nbsp;
away. Season 7 was the beginning of the end for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.820
Beckett and Castle's relationship, as they&nbsp;
were constantly tested and pulled apart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:52.260
almost as though the writers were no longer&nbsp;
planning to have them end up together. Which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:55.320
well, they weren't. The writers&nbsp;
planned to kill Beckett off.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:00.120
Before leaving Castle, Marlowe described&nbsp;
the series as "a love story wrapped in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:05.040
procedural." However, Seasons 7 and 8 veered&nbsp;
drastically from that concept. The show began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.520
to focus more on the character of Castle&nbsp;
and how he flourished without Beckett.

00:06:08.756 --> 00:06:13.920
Will they/won't they relationships are staples in&nbsp;
television; think The Vampire Diaries, Scandal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:18.420
or even Friends. Audiences yearn for these&nbsp;
couples to wake up and get together. From&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:22.680
the first moment of Castle, it was clear that&nbsp;
Richard Castle was into Detective Kate Beckett.

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:28.260
"The guy is crazy about you, and despite&nbsp;
your little act, you're crazy about him."

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:33.900
Whether she was interested in him remained to be&nbsp;
seen. While it was obvious that the two would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:38.460
the endgame, their romance wasn't necessary.&nbsp;
While Castle and Beckett were the glue holding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:42.240
the series together, their relationship didn't&nbsp;
need to turn into Bones and Booth from another,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:46.320
similar cop drama, Bones. They could have&nbsp;
followed the Mulder and Scully model instead.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:49.980
The two didn't need to become a couple for&nbsp;
the show to work, especially since they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:53.400
separated by other romantic partners,&nbsp;
by the fear of admitting their feelings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:58.560
or by jobs in different cities. Beckett and&nbsp;
Castle hardly ever share scenes in Season 8,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.700
as Beckett's off taking part in a secret&nbsp;
mission. And don't even get us started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.280
on that time Castle straight-up&nbsp;
disappeared on their wedding day.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:07.148
"Kate. Kate, why are you shutting me out?"

00:07:07.148 --> 00:07:08.790
"Castle, I love you."

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.820
Because of all this drama, the couple's happy&nbsp;
ending feels rushed. Audiences rarely saw them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:21.780
happy together over eight seasons, so it's hard&nbsp;
to believe that, seven years later, things are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:25.727
picture perfect. Maybe the writers had the right&nbsp;
idea when they planned to kill Beckett off.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:29.460
The seven-year time jump tacked on&nbsp;
at the end of Season 8 meant to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:32.280
fans happy. After everything&nbsp;
Beckett and Castle go through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:36.420
the show does a 180 and lets them live out&nbsp;
their lives together happily ever after.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.980
"Every writer needs&nbsp;
inspiration. And I found mine."

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:45.840
This was the original concept for Castle's&nbsp;
first showrunner Andrew Marlowe. Marlowe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:49.680
stepped down after running Seasons 1 through 6.&nbsp;
He had some standout episodes during his time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:53.760
but it's Season 6 Episode 5 that&nbsp;
shines when considering the series end.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:57.480
The episode is titled "Time Will&nbsp;
Tell" and plays into one of Castle's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.480 --> 00:08:01.440
fantastical ideas surrounding a case.&nbsp;
He and Beckett encounter Simon Doyle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:05.580
who claims he's a time traveler sent back&nbsp;
to stop a terrible event from unfolding.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.800
"Look. I'm a temporal anthropologist. What we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:11.220
do is we travel back in time and we&nbsp;
study culturally significant eras."

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:16.140
Naturally, Castle is all in, while Beckett has no&nbsp;
time to engage with Doyle's apparent delusions.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:19.080
By the end of the episode, Doyle&nbsp;
shares with Castle that he and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.060
Beckett are married in the future with three kids.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.900
"Real charmer, that one. I&nbsp;
can't believe you marry her."

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:30.900
Beckett is a Senator and Castle is now an author&nbsp;
of "serious literature." While this is a fun way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:34.860
to end the episode, the time jump in the series&nbsp;
finale seemingly confirms Doyle's prediction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:39.847
At least, on the kid front, as Beckett is seen&nbsp;
chasing around three kids in her home with Castle.

00:08:39.847 --> 00:08:44.760
Poor ratings are usually the biggest driver for&nbsp;
giving a show the ax. If a series isn't bringing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:49.020
in enough viewers, it's not doing its job, and&nbsp;
networks use that as an excuse to cut ties with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:53.580
a series. While this can sometimes happen too&nbsp;
soon, as with Firefly, Castle is lucky enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:58.080
to have run for eight successful seasons, even&nbsp;
if some were praised more highly than others.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:02.220
According to CBR, the lower ratings from&nbsp;
Castle Season 8 heavily contributed to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:06.180
series being canceled. In fact, viewership&nbsp;
had been declining over the previous few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:09.540
seasons. It seems as though Season 8&nbsp;
was the final straw for the network,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:14.079
as they no longer had faith that the show&nbsp;
would bring in the big numbers that it used to.

00:09:14.079 --> 00:09:16.620
"I thought that you would –"

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:19.260
"Just take you back, in spite&nbsp;
of what you put me through."

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:26.760
Season 8 of Castle was averaging under 10&nbsp;
million viewers per episode. And if that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:30.000
sounds like a lot, the highest viewership&nbsp;
for the network at the same time was over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.860
13 million. Season 8 saw the show's lowest ever&nbsp;
numbers, which had been dropping significantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:38.580
since the new showrunners took over. This&nbsp;
could be a direct result of the show moving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:42.839
away from the Castle/Beckett romance&nbsp;
and more into a Castle-centric story.

00:09:42.839 --> 00:09:46.557
"It is time to get back in&nbsp;
the Richard Castle business."

00:09:46.557 --> 00:09:48.626
"Oh well, thank you. I'm flattered."

00:09:48.626 --> 00:09:53.100
Due to the decline in viewership, Castle was&nbsp;
slated for major budget cuts if Season 9 were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:57.660
to move forward. According to CBR, the only way&nbsp;
another season of Castle would have been greenlit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:02.280
was if the show were able to significantly reduce&nbsp;
the amount of money it was spending on production.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:08.340
"The studio goes and casts the "braless&nbsp;
coed in blood-soaked t-shirt" from Knife 2?"

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:10.920
This may have contributed to Stana&nbsp;
Katic's dismissal from the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:14.820
as both Katic and co-star Tamala&nbsp;
Jones, who played Dr. Lanie Parish,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:20.100
were asked not to return for Season 9. According&nbsp;
to CinemaBlend, in 2016 Katic was revealed to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:24.180
one of the highest-paid actresses on television.&nbsp;
This would have been right around the time Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:28.860
8 of Castle was filming. Katic's negotiated&nbsp;
salary landed her at approximately $12 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:33.360
per season, based on the one-year contract&nbsp;
she signed after filming wrapped on Season 7.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.900
With budget cuts looming, and plans&nbsp;
on moving the story away from Castle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:41.460
and Beckett's romance, cutting out a $12&nbsp;
million+ salary is one sure way to do it.

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:45.960
Unfortunately for the crew, this wasn't&nbsp;
enough, and Castle was still canceled. Luckily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:49.080
Beckett and Castle got the ending&nbsp;
they deserved — which happens to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:52.560
be the one that original showrunner&nbsp;
Andrew Marlowe always envisioned.

